After all that you said, I only have one thing to disagree with you 
on. And that is that Tic Tac Toe is far easier to learn than tag. I've 
tried to teach many kids how to play tag, and almost without fail the 
very first time a kid plays tag he either thinks that he is always it 
or never it. IE: If he thinks he's always it, he runs and tags one 
person, then he goes and runs and tags anouther. If he thinks he's 
never it, tag is just a run away from you game. Tic Tac Toe on the 
other hand seems to be far easier for me to teach people. Matter of 
fact it's so easy that they quickly learn that if you play right 
nobody ever wins.

Anyways, as for if Nethack is hard to learn or not, I would have to 
say no it's not. I managed to even teach my dad how to play Nethack, 
and he is by no means a gamer or some grand person with computers. 
He's even learned how to Save Scum all on his own (despite that I tell 
him that's cheating). So I do agree that using the word hard isn't 
perhaps the best word to use. Complex does work alot better.
